A tree that breaks the relative param floor, adds a global risky pair and
matches a hold, run without LINKCLEAN_BASE_DIR: those parts are skipped with
one log line each, as is every other base-relative part. With a base the
same tree fails all three. Without one, a broken absolute floor still fails
Counts and a changed golden (a) row still fails Golden.
-- ops --
drop-global 40
jappend rules/brave/clean-urls.json [{"include": "*://*/*"}, "params"] "id"
relock
-- head/rules/acks.json --
{"schema": 1, "acks": [], "holds": [
  {"file": "brave-lists/clean-urls.json", "sha256": "${sha:rules/brave/clean-urls.json}",
   "expires": "2026-11-15", "reason": "fixture hold", "by": "fixture"}
]}
-- ops --
base none
run Counts
pass
logcount 1 skipped (no LINKCLEAN_BASE_DIR): Counts relative floor
logcount 1 skipped (no LINKCLEAN_BASE_DIR): Counts debounce include-drop limit
run Risky
pass
logcount 1 skipped (no LINKCLEAN_BASE_DIR): Risky
run Provenance
pass
logcount 1 skipped (no LINKCLEAN_BASE_DIR): Provenance acks-changed check
logcount 1 skipped (no LINKCLEAN_BASE_DIR): Provenance hold match
logcount 1 skipped (no LINKCLEAN_BASE_DIR): Provenance Upstream checks
run Golden/c
pass
logcount 1 skipped (no LINKCLEAN_BASE_DIR): Golden (c)
run Schema
pass
nolog skipped
run Compile
nolog skipped

# The same tree with a base: each skipped part was a real failure.
base real
run Counts
fail Counts relative floor: union.global_params
run Risky
fail Risky: new global pair (global, id)
run Provenance
fail held: brave-lists/clean-urls.json ${short:rules/brave/clean-urls.json} (fixture hold, expires 2026-11-15)

# Without a base, an absolute floor and a golden (a) row still fail.
base none
-- head/rules/brave/query-filter.json --
[]
-- ops --
relock
run Counts
fail query-filter: 0 rules / 0 params, floors 3 / 57
replace testdata/golden/positive.txtar "want: https://example.com/?id=7#top" "want: https://example.com/?id=8#top"
run Golden/a
fail 2 [keep]
